## 🐞 4. Database Naming Bug

The problem was caused by values written by the handler not matching the values allowed by the database constraints.

### Before → After

| Field             | Before                | After                |
| ----------------- | --------------------- | -------------------- |
| `action_taken`    | `blocked` / `allowed` | `BLOCKED` / `PASSED` |
| `triggered_layer` | `layer_1` / `None`    | `LAYER_1` / `NONE`   |

The allowed values are defined by the **SRS**, so the implementation must follow those exact values.

