# 📚 What I Learned

## 1. 📖 Read the SRS First

The task description did not contain all the database values.

The SRS defines values such as:

```text
PASSED
BLOCKED
REDACTED

NONE
LAYER_1
LAYER_2
LAYER_3
```

I initially implemented the correct logic but used the wrong database values.

### Lesson

> **Before writing values that interact with the database, check the SRS and database model first.**

---

## 2. 🧪 Mocks Can Hide Real Bugs

My tests mocked:

```python
write_threat_log()
```

Because of that, the database never validated the values.

The real PostgreSQL database immediately exposed the problem through its:

```text
CHECK constraints
NOT NULL constraints
```

### Lesson

> **Mocks are useful for unit testing, but they cannot replace testing against the real database.**

---

## 3. ⚡ FastAPI Background Tasks

I learned an important behavior around background logging.

For the blocked response, I used:

```python
JSONResponse(...)
```

instead of raising:

```python
HTTPException(...)
```

This allows the background threat-log task to run before the response lifecycle completes.

